      'Turn-flow example: 1. **Initial Deal**: 7 cards face down. 1st betting round. 2. **Round of 3**: Every player passes 3 cards from their hand to the player on their left. 2nd betting round. 3. **Round of 2**: Every player passes 2 cards to the player on their right. 3rd betting round. 4. **Round of 1**: Every player passes 1 card to the player on their left. 4th betting round. 5. **Selection**: Players choose their best 5 cards and discard the remaining 2 face down (these are dead). 6. **The Arrangement**: Players arrange their 5 chosen cards in a face-down pile in the order they wish to reveal them. 7. **The Rollout**: Each player reveals their first card simultaneously. Betting occurs. Then the second card, and so on, with betting after every reveal.',
